# Architecture Plan

## Product Scope

The app is an existing minimal single-page email sender. The only remaining
work item is issue #17: replace the flat page background with the specified
layered, colorful gradient while keeping the email form readable and its layout
unchanged.

## Module Structure

- `src/client/App.tsx`: one-page email sender UI and form state.
- `src/client/styles.css`: global visual system, responsive layout, form
  contrast, and the page-level gradient background for issue #17.
- `src/client/sendEmail.ts`: browser client for the same-origin send endpoint.
- `src/shared/email.ts`: request and response types shared by client/server.
- `src/server/`: Express app, send route, and server-side email service adapter.
- `tests/`: validation, email adapter, and end-to-end send-flow coverage.

## Issue Dependencies

1. Issue #17 depends on the existing page shell and stylesheet only.
2. It does not change the send endpoint, email provider integration, auth,
   persistence, shared DTOs, or tests.

## Key Design Decisions

- Implement the background as layered CSS gradients on the root/page surface:
  soft red and purple radial glows over a 135-degree yellow-to-aqua-to-lavender
  linear gradient.
- Preserve the existing dark global text color and Inter-based font stack.
- Leave the white form surface, input backgrounds, button colors, and status
  colors intact so controls remain legible against the new background.
- Keep the change stylesheet-only and avoid altering layout or application
  behavior.
